From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roman Leventov <leventov.ru@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 11:25:34 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 10/15] gc: prepare reusable heaps and reclaim transient
 storage

Expose numeric heap/collection statistics and mutator-boundary prepared
heap, dynamic-allocation and young-reclamation interfaces. Distinguish
verified empty payload from live storage, defer young-only maintenance
when old-generation progress is needed, and preserve finalization and
ordinary collector authority.

Describe ordinary literal shapes in generated units, prepare their
classes and property maps, and root those layouts in per-unit GC storage.
Keep ordinary, typed and private layouts distinct. Populate descendants
before parents to preserve lookup storage through later construction.

Visit newly inserted native roots during young collection while full
tracing and compaction retain complete scans. Reclaim empty managed
weak-slot chunks at the mutator boundary and account for their actual
storage. Avoid rewriting unchanged pointers and calling disabled
allocation instrumentation on the release fast path; retain debug IP
validation and enabled allocation/sampling tracking.

Carry root, weak-slot, prepared-layout and young-reclamation fixtures with
the corresponding runtime and generated ABI changes.
